      "id": "summary",
      "proposition": {
        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>Charging industry and electric vehicle manufacturers say measure could cost jobs and harm UK automotive sector </p><p>The UK government’s plans to <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/jun/14/uk-poised-water-down-2030-ev-sales-targets-industry-union-pressure\">further weaken electric car targets</a> have provoked a furious backlash from the charging industry and the electric car brand Polestar, which would lose out from the changes.</p><p>The government is expected to dilute rules known as the zero emission vehicle (ZEV) mandate. Government sources have said it will reduce a target for pure electric cars from 80% of all sales by 2030 to 50%.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/jun/15/backlash-uk-plans-weaken-ev-sales-targets-electric-vehicle-manufacturers-automotive-sector\">Continue reading...</a>"
